<title>GUATEMALA: Guatemala Jan coffee exports up 45 pct over yr ago.</title>
<headline>Guatemala Jan coffee exports up 45 pct over yr ago.</headline>
<dateline>GUATEMALA CITY 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Guatemala exported 514,269 60-kilo bags of coffee in January, the National Coffee Association (Anacafe) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The 45 percent increase over January 1996 exports of 355,797 bags was due to favorable prices, not to a larger harvest, Anacafe president Julio Arrivillaga told Reuters.  </p>
<p>&quot;We're high. I think this is because prices were higher and it was attractive to sell, to liquidate coffee and pay off loans,&quot; Arrivillaga said.</p>
<p>Guatemala exported 3.7 million 60-kilo bags of coffee in the 1995-1996 harvest and Anacafe predicts 3 million bags for the current harvest.</p>
<p>January exports were 16 percent higher than in December when 443,155 60-kilo bags of coffee were exported.</p>
<p>((--Fiona Ortiz, Guatemala City bureau +502 251-5718))</p>
